 #:seon.task{:name "a-red-prepare-leaks-its-candidate-branch"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A prepare whose proofs are red leaves its candidate branch (:merge-<id>) in the store's branches; only a successful accept retires it, so each refused review leaks one branch. Done when the candidate's lifetime is the merge task's: retired when the task closes (accepted or declined) or when a new prepare replaces it."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge! seon.cluster.source/accept-merge!}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/specs/merge.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-launch-option-change-in-deps-edn-refuses-every-check"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.cluster.source/dependency-digests` hashes deps.edn's whole bytes, so classify-paths refuses RESTART NEEDED for a change to an alias's :jvm-opts alone, which loads no different dependency (2026-10-08, lane dials-16gb: removing -XX:MaxRAMPercentage from :dev/:test was refused by bin/seon check on default twice, once right after a fresh restart). No deps.edn change can then pass bin/lane commit, because default only ever runs committed bytes. The class cache already keys on deps.edn without launch options (`seon.dev.dependency-digest/dependency-declarations`). Done when a deps.edn change confined to launch options (:jvm-opts :main-opts :exec-fn :exec-args :ns-default :ns-aliases) publishes and a dependency change still refuses, as a regression."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/dependency-digests seon.cluster.source/classify-paths}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-dependency-addition-cannot-be-proven-with-its-first-consumer"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.cluster.source/classify-paths` refuses RESTART NEEDED for any changed deps.edn in a candidate, so bin/seon check cannot prove a slice that adds a dependency together with the code that needs it (2026-10-08, lane impl-ref1: REF-1 adds commonmark-ext-heading-anchor and commonmark-ext-yaml-front-matter for the new `seon.ref`; the check refused before booting its throwaway JVM). The throwaway JVM launches from the candidate archive's own classpath (`clojure -Spath` in the archive), so it could load the new jars; only the rehearsal on default cannot. The slice then waits for root to commit deps.edn alone and restart default before its proof runs. Done when a candidate adding a Maven dependency and a namespace importing its classes passes bin/seon check with that namespace's test, and default's publication still refuses until restart, as a regression."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/classify-paths}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-candidate-script-namespace-is-analyzed-as-the-running-jvms-copy"
             :kind :function
             :intent "bin/seon check rehearses a candidate on default, and seon.fn.analyzer lints the checkout's non-program roots (script/) from the running JVM's own source directory, not the candidate's. A candidate that adds a var to seon.operator and a test/ deftest calling it is refused 'Unresolved var: `seon.operator/launch-argv`' (2026-10-08, lane dials-16gb), so no script change can land with its JVM test in one slice. Done when the rehearsal analyzes the candidate's script/ files and that pair passes, as a regression."
             :must-read #{seon.fn.analyzer/ensure-dependency-analysis! seon.cluster/rehearse-source!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-second-write-back-conflicts-with-the-branchs-own-first"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Lane repl-only-2 (default 35e95e7b3, 2026-10-09) wrote its branch back with `my.program/write-branch!` (adding `my.program-test/an-agent-reads-and-writes-files-as-clojure-does`), redefined that test on the branch, and a second `write-branch!` refused :conflict: `:seon.program/conflict-digests` named base `:seon.program/absent`, head = the digest its own first write-back put in the file, branch = the new one. The write-back base does not advance past the branch's own write, so iterating on a written-back declaration needs an outside edit. Done when a second write-back of the same branch replaces what its first wrote, with a regression."
             :must-read #{my.program/write-branch! seon.cluster.source/write-back!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "merge-base-survives-collection"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.cluster.source/merge-base` reads the immutable commit held by `seon.cluster.registry/base-branch` through `datahike.api/commit-as-db`, preserving attributes without history. `seon.cluster.registry/fork!` creates that branches ref at the fork point (a nested fork inherits its parent's base toward the same target), `seon.cluster.registry/advance-base!` advances it to the accepted source value, and `seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch!` deletes it with its work branch. `datahike.gc/reachable-in-branch` always retains heads and their indexes; remove-before limits only parents. Missing fork entities or mismatched targets still refuse. Reused names receive fresh refs. Proofs: `seon.merge-test/a-base-ref-keeps-the-fork-commit-only-until-retirement`, `seon.merge-test/the-merge-base-retains-the-count-needed-by-add`, the existing registry retention and branch-name reuse tests, and nested merge comparison."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/merge-base seon.cluster.source/compare-branch seon.cluster.source/accept-merge! seon.cluster.registry/fork! seon.cluster.registry/branch-fork-entity seon.cluster.registry/fork-of seon.cluster.registry/retention-cutoff}}
 #:seon.task{:name "write-back-of-a-new-require-analyses-the-published-snapshot"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A `require` added to a test namespace's ns form at the REPL is refused by `my.program/write-branch!` (lane loop-prove, 86b7cdbbe, 2026-10-10) as \"Unresolved namespace seon.db\": `seon.cluster.source/write-back!` proves the candidate by analysing it (`seon.cluster.source/proven-file`, `seon.fn.analyzer/invoke-kondo`) against the published HEAD snapshot (data/source/<sha>), whose analysis lacks the namespaces the branch's own new require makes reachable, so a require the branch is adding cannot resolve. Not verified at the REPL here (the repro writes a file); the sibling `seon.turn.batch-test/a-repl-require-is-written-back-in-the-ns-form-and-reindexes-equal` proves the plain case calling `write-back!` directly. Done when a branch that adds a require to an ns form and a form using it writes back and reindexes equal, asserted on the written paths."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/write-back! seon.cluster.source/proven-file my.program/write-branch! seon.fn.analyzer/invoke-kondo}}
 #:seon.task{:name "held-digests-refuses-a-map-on-the-write-back-path"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An open fault on default a6cbe4fcf (2026-10-10, runtime_status): `seon.cluster.source/held-digests` refused its result at `[[:seon.program/sym seon.sci.forgive/scan]]`, \"expected :seon.program/definition-digest (a string of length exactly 64), got a map\", contract `:seon.source/expected-digests`, called from `seon.cluster.source/write-back-commits`. A write-back whose accepted merge holds that identity fails before any file is read; the identity attribute `:seon.program/sym` is not one of `:seon.fn/sym`, `:seon.test/sym`, `:seon.ns/name`. Not reproduced by lane merge-path. Done when the producer of that accepted identity is found and `held-digests` answers a digest per identity, with a regression."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/held-digests seon.cluster.source/write-back-commits seon.cluster.source/write-back!}}

 #:seon.task{:name "accepting-a-one-function-merge-allocates-hundreds-of-megabytes"
  :kind :function
  :intent "`seon.cluster.source/accept-merge!` of a one-function, one-test proposal (lane merge-path, 2026-10-10, default a6cbe4fcf, gate run e5d251ed2dd7) allocated 733 MB in 322 ms when accepted and 2.0 GB when it refused (custody mismatch). What the work must do: check the touched entities' digests, transact the selected declarations onto the target and record the merge, proportional to the declarations merged, not to the program. Profile the accept with `seon.profile/measure`, name the armed functions that allocate, and fix the owner; done when a one-function accept allocates within 10x of its datoms' size. Chain run 5 (2026-10-10, default 340462543, the one-function proposal `my.program/match-row`, gate run 74e4621e2005) measured the whole merge, so the task covers prepare too: `seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge!` 4.0 s and 1.1 GB; `seon.cluster.source/accept-merge!` 1.0 s and 1.4 GB; root's reaching-test step after the accept 2.5 s and 2.2 GB. Each is over the one-second line (CLAUDE.md: name the armed functions that account for it, or fix it) and none is proportional to the declarations merged; profile all three, prepare first."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/accept-merge! seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge!}
  :evidence #{"docs/seon/plan.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-never-run-on-the-target-is-not-blamed-on-the-merge"
  :kind :function
  :intent "The first automatic landing (merge task fa08193bc6b9, 2026-10-10, gate run 2da09057317d) was refused `:seon.source/red-test-error` for 11 reached tests: 10 are red on main's unchanged program too, and the 11th erred in the gate on an interpreter defect. `seon.cluster.source/red-test-verdicts` reads the absence of a result on the target as not red. Root fix B (one gate evaluator, fable-replan section 4.3): `seon.cluster.source/accept-merge!` judges the merge branch's reached tests and main's under the same evaluation in the same gate run, so a verdict is one predicate (red at the gate and not red on main at the gate's evaluator) with no tiers, no `:unverified` and no separate run on the target. Done when this task's proof passes with that one predicate."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/red-test-verdicts seon.cluster.source/red-test-refusal seon.cluster.source/accept-merge! seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge! seon.test.runner/red-at-current-reach?}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/fable-replan.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agents-repl-scratch-namespace-never-blocks-its-landing"
  :kind :function
  :intent "Agent r7-problems-prose (merge task 15b7e49ebafb, 2026-10-10) required `seon.problems` from its `user` namespace; `seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge!` took that `[:seon.ns/name user]` row into the delta, `seon.cluster.source/proven-files` found no file for it and the landing refused `:one-file`. The filter that dropped such rows at prepare (ab18c3ffc) was a fence and is reverted. Root design: an agent's REPL scratch namespace is never program, so the evaluation that writes its row never writes it as a program declaration and `seon.cluster.source/compare-branch` never sees it. Done when this task's proof lands the change alone with no filter at prepare."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge! seon.cluster.source/compare-branch seon.cluster.source/proven-files}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-docstring-only-change-lands-without-interpreting-its-namespace"
  :kind :function
  :intent "Root's direct seon.cluster.source/land! (deleted) of merge task 15b7e49ebafb (proposal d27b6032aa2e, agent r7-problems-prose, default ab18c3ffc, 2026-10-11, lane first-live-land) passed prepare and was refused at `seon.cluster.source/accept-merge!` as `:seon.source/red-test-error` (run b90587aa1a2f, 19.1 s): eight tests `:red` (green on main) and `seon.error-test/error-identity-and-occurrences-are-owned-by-the-writer` `:red-on-target`. The change is docstring-only: `seon.problems/deferred-agents`, `seon.problems/error-signatures`, `seon.problems/ai-prose` and `seon.problems/failed-tests` differ from main only by dates and counts removed from their docstrings, yet their definition digests differ, so the merge branch interprets them and the reached tests run against interpreted `seon.problems`. Reproduced as agent first-live-land by re-evaluating only the docstring-only `seon.problems/failed-tests` (run b97ef3733299): `seon.problems-test/a-resolved-fault-stays-closed-until-it-recurs` errors with `seon.db/db` refused argument nil inside `(found connection)`, and `seon.instrument-test/an-output-refusal-names-the-function-that-returned-it` errors with `:malli.core/invalid-schema` (schema nil) from `seon.schema/contract-product`. Two owners: (1) a declaration whose behavior digest is unchanged (`seon.test/behavior-differences` already treats a docstring-only change as none) keeps its compiled Var on the branch instead of being interpreted, so such a change lands; (2) the interpreted-only reds themselves belong to the interpreted-tier tasks (`seon.sci.eval/remaining-interpreted-only-test-differences`). Done when re-landing 15b7e49ebafb (or any docstring-only proposal) is accepted with the reached tests green and the four docstrings land in `src/seon/problems.clj`."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/accept-merge! seon.test/behavior-differences seon.sci.eval/bind-lazy-members! seon.sci.eval/interpret-overlay! seon.problems/failed-tests}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agents-scratch-schema-never-rides-its-landing"
  :kind :function
  :intent "Agent r8-problems-prose evaluated `:seon.problems/qty` (`[:int {:min 1}]`) from its `user` namespace while working (2026-10-10T17:45:06Z) and never used it; `seon.cluster.source/compare-branch` lists it as an addition, so seon.cluster.source/land! (deleted) of merge task 57ad6cd33297 would write an unused schema into `resources/seon/schemas/seon.problems.edn`. Same root as `seon.cluster.source/an-agents-repl-scratch-namespace-never-blocks-its-landing`: what an agent evaluates in its scratch namespace is never program, so it never enters the diff; no filter at prepare."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge! seon.cluster.source/compare-branch seon.cluster.source/proven-schema-file}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-landing-writes-git-objects-with-a-parent-compare-and-swap"
  :kind :function
  :intent "Fence outside the night (no-fences law, AGENTS.md 2026-10-11): `seon.cluster.source/commit!` (0e502a59e) and `bin/lane commit` serialize on `.git/lane-commit.lock` and recheck proven bytes, because a landing writes into the shared working tree that lanes edit. Root fix A (fable-replan section 4.3): seon.cluster.source/land! (deleted) writes the proven bytes as git objects (`git hash-object`, `git update-index --cacheinfo` on a private index, `git write-tree`, `git commit-tree`) and advances the branch with `git update-ref` compare-and-swap on the expected parent, never touching the shared tree; git's own exclusion replaces the lock. Done when `seon.cluster.merge-test/a-landing-commit-waits-for-the-lane-commit-lock` is deleted with the lock and a landing commits while a lane holds uncommitted edits in the same file, leaving them untouched."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/commit! seon.cluster.source/write-back!}
  :evidence #{"bin/lane" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/fable-replan.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-write-back-root-is-valid-by-its-schema"
  :kind :function
  :intent "Fence outside the night (no-fences law): `seon.cluster.source/write-back!` and `seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge!` refuse `:root-refused` at call time when the root is not an absolute checkout outside data/source (93d9e4ef6), a check beside the mechanism. Root design: the checkout root is a configuration dial (`:seon.config.fs/working-root`) whose Malli schema admits only an absolute existing checkout directory, validated once where the configuration is applied, and the write-back request schema (`:seon.source/write-back-request`) names that schema; the runtime refusal and its enum value go."
  :must-read #{seon.cluster.source/write-back! seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge! seon.config/defaults}}]
